  "translation": "Tonight, my dad and I are making dinner together. Dad can stir-fry, and I can cook rice. We first take out vegetables and meat from the fridge. Mom asks us: 'What do you need?' Dad says: 'Need some salt and oil.' I washed three potatoes and two carrots. While Dad was cutting vegetables, I watched beside him. He cuts very fast, and I admire him. Later, we stir-fried together. This dish is very fragrant; I couldn't help but taste a bite. Mom also said it was delicious. We, as a family, ate very happily. After finishing the meal, I voluntarily washed the dishes. Mom praised me for growing up."
